---
// PILLAR — Educational Leader. The earliest chronological pillar, so it sits
// before Premier Leadership.
//
// SECTION OPENING: the LEDE leads. About above it opens on body copy (the
// drop cap) and PillarPremier below it opens on its kicker, so neither
// neighbour is matched. This is also the one pillar with no photograph — the
// lede at full display scale is what stands in for the opening image, which
// is exactly the case the lede rule exists for.
//
// No image, deliberately. The page already carries a heavy photo load by this
// point (portrait band, about inset, seated portrait) and the live margin plus
// the vertical rhythm carry this section instead.
//
// Contact: the district WEBSITE is published; her district EMAIL is not. That
// address is her public-school-district employer address and it does not
// belong on a commercial consulting page. Final client decision, not a
// placeholder. The address itself is deliberately not written anywhere in
// this tree, comments included, so a grep for it stays clean.
---

<section class="education spread" id="sec-education">
  <!-- Columns 2-10 — the same break PillarPremier's lede takes, so the two
       ledes rhyme even though the sections open differently. -->
  <p class="pillar-lede">Education should not simply require students to fit into systems; strong systems must also be willing to evolve to meet the needs of the students they serve.</p>

  <div class="education-head">
    <h2 class="pillar-kicker">Educational Leader</h2>
    <p class="pillar-role">Alternative Education High School Principal</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pillar-body">
    <!-- Paragraph 1 ends at "traditional measures." The rest of the client's
         sentence is detached upward into the lede above and is not repeated. -->
    <p>For more than two decades, Dr.&nbsp;Syreeta McClain has dedicated her career to seeing possibility in young people&mdash;especially those whose potential may not always be recognized through traditional measures.</p>
    <p>Her expertise in customized high school programming, alternative education, student engagement, and leadership has allowed her to create pathways for students navigating complex academic and life circumstances. Through innovation, technology, collaboration, compassion, and unwavering advocacy, Dr.&nbsp;McClain works to build educational environments where students are seen, supported, challenged, and prepared for what comes next.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- A CODA, not a pull quote: it stays inside the body measure (3-8) and
       does not break out of it. There is exactly one pull quote on this page
       and it is the chapter break. -->
  <p class="pillar-coda">At the heart of her leadership is a simple belief: meet students where they are, without losing sight of where they are capable of going.</p>

  <!-- Live margin. Last in source order so that when the grid collapses it
       falls inline in reading order, after the copy rather than before it. -->
  <aside class="education-margin">
    <p class="margin-label">District</p>
    <a class="margin-link" href="https://www.ucvts.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ucvts.org</a>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  .education{ padding-top: var(--vr-standard); }

  /* Explicit rows. The lede leads; the margin hangs beside the body copy. */
  .pillar-lede      { grid-column: 2 / 11; grid-row: 1; }
  .education-head   { grid-column: 3 / 9;  grid-row: 2; }
  .pillar-body      { grid-column: 3 / 9;  grid-row: 3; }
  .pillar-coda      { grid-column: 3 / 9;  grid-row: 4; }
  .education-margin { grid-column: 9 / 13; grid-row: 3; }

  /* Type treatment copied from PillarPremier's .pillar-lede verbatim — same
     size, weight, line-height, tracking and Fraunces axes. No value is new. */
  .pillar-lede{
    margin: 0 0 var(--vr-tight);
    font-family: var(--display);
    /* Lede tier — opsz 72, wght 350, SOFT 35, WONK 0. */
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-lede);
    font-weight: 350;
    font-size: clamp(27px, 3.6vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .education-head{ margin-bottom: var(--s5); }

  .pillar-kicker{
    margin: 0 0 var(--s3);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    letter-spacing: 0.26em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
  }

  /* The hairline sits between the lede and the label, so it reads as the rule
     that closes the lede rather than as decoration above the section. */
  .pillar-kicker::before{
    content: "";
    display: block;
    width: 40px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--hair-strong);
    margin-bottom: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
  }

  .pillar-role{
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.1vw, 14px);
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* Body metrics copied from PillarPremier's .pillar-body verbatim. */
  .pillar-body{
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    letter-spacing: 0.004em;
    color: var(--slate);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .pillar-body p{ margin: 0; }
  .pillar-body p + p{ margin-top: 1.5em; }

  /* Intermediate scale — ~1.9x the body, ~0.58x the lede, so it is plainly
     larger than the paragraphs and plainly smaller than the display line.
     The OPEN step above it. That step is the chapter break's own, but the
     break spends it TWICE (margin + padding), so it stays the largest gap on
     the page by roughly 2x and this does not compete with it. */
  .pillar-coda{
    margin: var(--vr-open) 0 0;
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-family: var(--display);
    /* Coda tier — opsz 48, wght 360, SOFT 45, WONK 0. */
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-coda);
    font-weight: 360;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.1vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.42;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* --- Marginalia: one labelled link in the live margin ----------- */
  /* Dropped well down the measure so its top edge does not line up with the
     body copy beside it — that alignment is what makes a margin read as a
     second column. */
  .education-margin{
    margin-top: clamp(72px, 9vw, 150px);
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: var(--s3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }

  .margin-label{
    margin: 0 0 var(--s2);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    line-height: 1.9;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* Slate at FULL opacity. At 0.72 this measured 3.81:1 on Porcelain, under
       the 4.5:1 AA floor for 9.5px text. The step below the Obsidian link it
       labels is carried by colour and size, which is enough — it does not need
       an opacity knock-down that costs legibility. */
    color: var(--slate);
  }

  /* A text link, not a button: the margin carries references, and a solid
     fill out here would outweigh the section it sits beside. Underlined at
     rest so it never depends on colour alone to read as a link. */
  .margin-link{
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.05vw, 14px);
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--hair-strong);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 6px;
    transition: color 320ms var(--ease),
                text-decoration-color 320ms var(--ease),
                transform 320ms var(--ease);
  }

  .margin-link:hover,
  .margin-link:focus-visible{
    color: var(--slate);
    text-decoration-color: var(--obsidian);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .margin-link:active{ transform: translateY(0); }
  .margin-link:focus-visible{ outline: 1px solid var(--slate); outline-offset: 6px; }

  /* ---- One stacked column. The 12-column grid does not exist here. ---- */
  @media (max-width: 1024px){
    .pillar-lede,
    .education-head,
    .pillar-body,
    .pillar-coda,
    .education-margin{ grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: auto; }

    .pillar-body{ max-width: none; }
    .pillar-coda{ max-width: none; }

    /* Collapses INLINE in reading order — it is last in source order, so it
       lands after the coda. Not a sidebar, not hidden. */
    .education-margin{ margin-top: var(--vr-tight); }
  }
</style>
